API Gateway — 35-Minute PhD-Level HLD Presentation
Competition preparation • Research depth • Production implementation • Architecture trade-offs • Senior architect communication

Your goal should be to present the API Gateway 
not merely as a routing component, 
but as a critical distributed-systems boundary whose design affects latency, 
availability, security, scalability, fault isolation, and operational complexity.

To make this competitive at a research-presentation level, 
we will structure it around a clear engineering problem, 
explicit design choices, alternative architectures, quantitative reasoning,
implementation details, failure scenarios, and defensible trade-offs. 

A PhD-level presentation should also distinguish established engineering principles from hypotheses that would require experimental validation.

