What to say — approximately 1 minute

            “Good morning, everyone.

            Today, I will present the high-level design of an API Gateway for a distributed microservices platform.
            
            The interesting problem is not simply how to forward an HTTP request. 
            It is how to introduce a common entry point without making that entry point a bottleneck or a single point of failure.
            
            Every request may pass through authentication, 
            routing, rate limiting, observability, and sometimes caching or protocol transformation. 
            These capabilities improve consistency, but they also introduce computational overhead and new failure modes.
            
            My design therefore focuses on three questions: 
                  what belongs in the gateway, 
                  how the gateway remains resilient under load and partial failure, 
                  and how we validate that the resulting architecture meets measurable service-level objectives.”
            
            Competition advantage: Open with a research question and measurable evaluation dimensions, 
                                  rather than starting with a list of components.




