Slide 7 — data plane versus control plane
Dimension	                        Data plane	                                              Control plane
Responsibility	                  Processes live requests	                                  Defines and distributes configuration
Typical operations	              Authentication checks, routing, rate-limit decisions	    Route updates, policy changes, certificate/configuration distribution
Latency sensitivity	              Directly affects request latency	                        Usually affects changes and convergence
Failure concern	                  Request failures and traffic overload	                    Stale configuration or failed updates
Design principle	                Keep the request path efficient	                          Validate changes before publishing them

Key insight: A control-plane outage should not automatically stop all traffic.
A well-designed gateway can continue using its last known valid configuration, 
subject to expiry, revocation, and security requirements.



